From: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: refill the RX ring when it runs out of host descriptors

RX_NO_CPU_DSCP is enabled in the QDMA interrupt banks, but the handler only
clears that status and never wakes the NAPI poll.  A ring that a failed
refill left empty therefore never receives again: no RX_DONE follows, the
poll that would recycle descriptors and refill the ring never runs, and the
PON MAC MBI RX FIFO overruns behind the idle ring (fifo=0x180, int=0x8000)
until the box is rebooted.

Treat the event as a NAPI wakeup, as the vendor QDMA driver does in
qdma_bmgr/eth_lan: RX_NO_CPU_DSCP is a level condition and the refill
clears it by itself, so the interrupt stays enabled.

Signed-off-by: naoki66 <naoki66@qq.com>
---
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_eth.c
@@ -1886,7 +1886,7 @@
 {
 	struct airoha_irq_bank *irq_bank = dev_instance;
 	struct airoha_qdma *qdma = irq_bank->qdma;
-	u32 rx_intr_mask = 0, rx_intr1, rx_intr2;
+	u32 rx_intr_mask = 0, rx_intr1, rx_intr2, rx_starve;
 	u32 intr[ARRAY_SIZE(irq_bank->irqmask)];
 	int i;
 
@@ -1911,6 +1911,25 @@
 		rx_intr_mask |= (rx_intr2 << 16);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * RX_NO_CPU_DSCP reports a ring that ran out of host descriptors.  It is
+	 * a level condition that stays asserted while the ring is empty, so it
+	 * has to wake the NAPI poll exactly like RX_DONE: the poll recycles the
+	 * completed descriptors and refills the ring.  Clearing the status only
+	 * leaves the ring empty, the ring never receives again and the PON MAC
+	 * MBI RX FIFO overruns behind it.  The interrupt stays enabled because
+	 * the refill clears the condition on its own.
+	 */
+	rx_starve = ((intr[1] & RX_NO_CPU_DSCP_LOW_INT_MASK) >>
+		     RX_NO_CPU_DSCP_LOW_OFFSET) |
+		    (intr[2] & RX_NO_CPU_DSCP_HIGH_INT_MASK);
+	if (rx_starve) {
+		dev_warn_ratelimited(qdma->eth->dev,
+				     "QDMA RX ring out of host descriptors (queues=0x%08x), refilling\n",
+				     rx_starve);
+		rx_intr_mask |= rx_starve;
+	}
+
 	for (i = 0; rx_intr_mask && i < ARRAY_SIZE(qdma->q_rx); i++) {
 		if (!qdma->q_rx[i].ndesc)
 			continue;
